 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Colours agree",
     "texto": [
      "The colour goes **after** the noun and **agrees** with it.\n\n- Colours in **-o** have four forms: **rojo, roja, rojos, rojas**. The same goes for amarillo, blanco, negro.\n- Colours in **-e** or a consonant have two forms, singular and plural: **verde, verdes**; **azul, azules**; **gris, grises**; **marrón, marrones**.\n- **Rosa** usually stays the same.\n\nUna falda **roja**, un jersey **verde**, unos zapatos **marrones**, unos vaqueros **azules**.\n\nTo ask: **¿De qué color es tu abrigo?** → **Es gris.**\n\nIf the garment is already known, you can leave it out: prefiero **el rosa** (= el vestido rosa)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The colour after the noun",
     "texto": [
      "Each colour follows its own pattern:\n\n- Colours in **-o**: four forms. **un jersey rojo**, **una falda roja**, **unos zapatos rojos**, **unas faldas rojas**.\n- Colours in **-e** or a consonant: two forms. **un abrigo verde**, **una falda verde**, **unos vaqueros azules**, **unos zapatos marrones**.\n- **Rosa** usually stays the same: **unos zapatos rosa**.\n\nThe colour goes **after** the noun, and the adjective **nuevo** behaves the same way: **una falda nueva**."
     ],
